{"type":"message","id":"c6ef9440","parentId":"3c2a2b6e","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:20.742Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me try reading the PDF with a different approach - just read the file without page filtering.","thinkingSignature":"541387a3fd2166a8a994a94d7c8a8f68c8aeefea75842907a42bce54a420790a"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_poli21s15rfo_1","name":"pdf","arguments":{"pdf":"/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/echo_simulator_design---7d0c67a8-2c32-42d6-8211-32f3f8453231.pdf","prompt":"详细阅读并总结这个文档的所有核心内容"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":411,"output":104,"cacheRead":44384,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":44899,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780230377373,"responseId":"066b5beaf5e7614cd22a9cfe27091ecb"}}
{"type":"message","id":"830e6ed5","parentId":"c6ef9440","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:34.090Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_poli21s15rfo_1","toolName":"pdf","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This document outlines a software design for an \"Echo System Simulator,\" a tool designed to model and analyze the dynamics of an AI-driven digital asset ecosystem. Here's a summary of its core contents:\n\n**1. Project Overview**\n\n*   **Background:** The project is motivated by the emerging AI era where users can create (Skills) and consume Skills, leading to a supply-demand economic relationship.\n*   **Core Concept:** The \"Echo System\" aims to package AI Skills as digital assets (\"Echo Resources\" or \"Echo Assets\") that can be traded, licensed, and further developed.\n*   **Simulator Goal:** To simulate the functioning of such an Echo System, exploring optimal economic rules (pricing, revenue sharing) to foster ecosystem prosperity.\n*   **Scope:**\n    *   **Simulated:** The lifecycle of Echo Resources, economic flows (supply, demand, pricing, payment), resource usage/derivation/extension, multi-agent behavior, and the impact of different rules on ecosystem prosperity.\n    *   **Not Simulated:** Underlying technologies of the Echo System's trusted data space (e.g., sandboxing) and the detailed implementation of system security.\n\n**2. Core Simulation Elements**\n\n*   **Key Terminology:** Defines terms like \"Echo Resource,\" \"Usage,\" \"Derivation,\" \"Extension,\" \"Trusted Data Space,\" \"Multi-Agent Simulation (ABM),\" and \"AI Agent.\"\n*   **Simulation Objects:**\n    *   **Echo Resources/Assets:** Characterized by attributes like ID, name, type, creator, content, pricing, licensing, relationships (parent, extensions), and status (circulation, holders, activity, value).\n    *   **Users (Agents):** Possess attributes like ID, role (producer/consumer), expertise, financial status, capabilities, economic details, and behavioral states (production, consumption, idle).\n*   **System State:** Tracks global economic indicators such as total economic volume, resource volume, transaction activity, prosperity index, and domain distribution.\n*   **Simulated Behaviors:**\n    *   **User Actions:** Producing Skills, consuming Skills, deriving new resources from existing ones, extending resources, externalizing resources (selling for external markets), making pricing decisions, and making purchasing decisions.\n    *   **Triggers:** These actions are triggered by market conditions, demand, supply, pricing, and agent capabilities.\n*   **Economic Flow Model:** Describes various transaction types: direct sales, subscriptions, revenue sharing from derivations and extensions, and external market income.\n*   **Adjustable Rules and Parameters:** Includes categories for pricing rules, licensing models, royalty splits (derivation/extension), copyright terms, platform fees, and credit mechanisms. These parameters directly influence simulation outcomes.\n*   **External Environment Parameters:** Considers factors like user base growth, resource type distribution, market demand fluctuations, technological maturity, and macroeconomic indicators.\n\n**3. System Architecture Design**\n\n*   **Overall Architecture:** A layered structure consisting of:\n    *   **Frontend Display Layer:** Presents system status, resource browsing, user views, and simulation playback.\n    *   **Backend Service Layer:** Houses the Multi-Agent Simulation Engine (Mesa), AI Agent Services (integrating LLMs), Rule Engine, and Data Analysis/Statistics.\n    *   **Data Storage Layer:** Manages relational databases, time-series data, and graph data.\n*   **Frontend Design Principles:** Focus on displaying data, prioritizing visualizations, real-time updates, and user-configurable views.\n*   **Frontend Modules:** Includes dashboards, resource browsers, user browsers, simulation playback, rule configuration panels, and analysis reports.\n*   **Frontend Technology Stack:** Recommends React/Vue 3, D3.js/ECharts/Three.js for visualization, and WebSocket for real-time communication.\n*   **Backend Design:**\n    *   **Multi-Agent Simulation Engine (Mesa):** Built on Python Mesa, it includes core components like the global model, base agents, user agents, resource agents, market agents, and system agents. It defines agent behaviors (produce, consume, derive, extend, externalize) and schedulers.\n    *   **AI Agent Services (LLM Integration):** Each user agent has an associated AI Agent that uses LLMs for decision-making. This involves prompt engineering to provide context (user state, market environment, history) and generating structured JSON outputs for decisions. LLM integration can use local models or APIs.\n    *   **Rule Engine:** Handles loading, validation, and management of simulation rules, including hot updates and A/B testing of rule sets.\n*   **Data Storage Design:**\n    *   **Relational Database (PostgreSQL/SQLite):** Stores user data, resource data, transaction records, authorization records, simulation step data, and rule configurations.\n    *   **Time-Series Database (InfluxDB/built-in TSDB):** Records global metrics, resource circulation, and user activity over time.\n    *   **Graph Database (Neo4j/in-memory graph):** Models relationships between resources, users, and transactions.\n    *   **Snapshot Storage:** For saving and restoring simulation states.\n\n**4. Key Algorithms and Models**\n\n*   **Prosperity Index Model:** A weighted combination of various factors like resource diversity, transaction volume, user satisfaction, creator income balance, resource circulation speed, and innovation rate. Weights are configurable.\n*   **Matching and Pricing Algorithms:**\n    *   **Demand-Supply Matching:** Based on domain similarity and price budget.\n    *   **Dynamic Pricing Suggestions:** Recommendations based on supply-demand ratios, competitor pricing, and historical transaction data.\n    *   **Auction Mechanisms:** Optional support for English, Dutch, and Vickrey auctions.\n*   **AI Agent Decision Flow:** A five-step process: perceive state, reason (LLM inference), evaluate feasibility, execute, and learn (optional).\n*   **External Market Model:** Defines functions for external demand, product quality, and external revenue based on these factors.\n\n**5. Performance and Scalability Requirements**\n\n*   **Scale Metrics:** Defines target requirements for simultaneous simulated resources, users, transactions per step, simulation speed, and snapshot recovery.\n*   **Performance Optimization Strategies:** Includes parallel computing, LLM batch processing, incremental UI updates, memory optimization, graph computation optimization, and snapshot compression.\n\n**6. Interface Design**\n\n*   **Frontend-Backend Interfaces:** RESTful APIs for simulation control, resource/user management, analytics, and rules configuration. WebSocket for real-time state updates.\n*   **LLM Service Interface:** An API for AI Agents to make decisions based on provided context.\n*   **Scenario Configuration System:** Allows for pre-defined scenarios (e.g., cold start, rapid growth, niche market) and custom scene configurations.\n\n**7. Development and Deployment**\n\n*   **Technology Stack Summary:** Details the chosen technologies for frontend, backend, databases, LLM integration, and deployment.\n*   **Project Structure:** Outlines the directory organization for frontend and backend code.\n*   **Deployment Modes:** Supports development mode (local, separated), single-machine mode (Docker Compose), and cluster mode (K8s for large-scale simulations).\n\n**8. Testing Strategy**\n\n*   **Testing Levels:** Covers unit tests, integration tests, API tests, end-to-end tests, and performance tests.\n*   **Simulation Validation:** Emphasizes logical consistency checks, sensitivity analysis of key parameters, and comparison with real-world data or academic literature.\n\n**9. Extension Plan**\n\n*   **MVP (Minimum Viable Product):** Focuses on a basic Mesa engine, initial dashboard, core agent behaviors, basic LLM integration, and single rule set simulation.\n*   **Mid-Term:** Scalability to more agents, full set of behaviors, simulation playback, multi-rule analysis, and LLM agent memory/learning.\n*   **Long-Term:** Further scaling, complex ecosystem simulations, automated rule optimization, 3D visualization, and advanced reporting.\n\n**10. Risks and Mitigation**\n\n*   Identifies risks such as high LLM costs/latency, performance limitations with many agents, uncontrollable LLM decisions, and large data storage pressure.\n*   Proposes mitigation strategies like batch processing, caching, multi-threading, prompt tuning, data compression, and automated cleanup.\n\n**11. Appendix**\n\n*   **Glossary:** References the key terminology defined earlier.\n*   **References:** Lists relevant documentation and literature.\n*   **Decision Records:** Explains key architectural choices, such as using Mesa, a decoupled frontend/backend, and LLMs for AI Agents.\n\nIn essence, this document provides a comprehensive blueprint for building a sophisticated simulation environment to understand the complex economic and behavioral dynamics of a future AI-powered digital asset marketplace."}],"details":{"model":"google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite","native":true,"pdf":"/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/echo_simulator_design---7d0c67a8-2c32-42d6-8211-32f3f8453231.pdf","attempts":[]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1780230394085}}
{"type":"message","id":"fff072bc","parentId":"830e6ed5","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:40.904Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user shared a PDF about the Echo System Simulator and asked me to read it. Now they've sent a reply saying \"[Replying to: \"[file message]\"] <p>阅读总结</p>\" which means they're asking me to summarize what I just read.\n\nWait, actually looking more carefully - they seem to be asking ME to summarize the PDF. But I already did that. Let me re-read...\n\nActually they sent a reply to the PDF message, and the body is \"阅读总结\" which means \"reading summary\". So they might be asking me to provide a summary, or they might be saying they want me to read and summarize something else.\n\nBut I already summarized the PDF in the previous turn. So this message might be them saying \"yes, summarize it\" as a confirmation, or they might want a different kind of summary.\n\nActually, looking at the context more carefully - the previous turn was me asking if they wanted me to reference the visual style from the PDF or if they had other reference images. Then they replied with \"[Replying to: \"[file message]\"] <p>阅读总结</p>\" - this seems to be a reply to the PDF file message, saying \"阅读总结\" (reading summary). So they might be asking me to summarize the PDF I just read.\n\nBut I already did provide a summary in the previous turn. So maybe they're just acknowledging the summary request and want me to present it better, or maybe they want a more concise version.\n\nActually wait - looking at the flow:\n1. User sent PDF\n2. I asked if they wanted me to reference the visual style\n3. User replied with \"阅读总结\" as a reply to the PDF message\n\nSo the user is probably saying \"yes, summarize the document\" - but I already did that in the previous turn. Maybe they didn't see it? Let me present the summary more clearly.\n\n\nI should organize this more cleanly for them.\n","thinkingSignature":"b9cf49b452f8553d2167ed56a34aafb89f3f2eb2c94e48b24f6c2a9d0c2a7702"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n看了，这是 **ECHO System Simulator** 的设计文档——一个 AI 数字资产生态的经济模拟器。\n\n核心内容：\n\n**目标**\n- 模拟 ECHO 资产协议的经济规则，测试最优定价/收益分配机制\n- 探索如何让生态繁荣\n\n**核心概念**\n- **Echo Resource**：可被交易、授权、再创作（派生/扩展）的 AI Skills 资产\n- **用户（Agent）**：可以是生产者或消费者，有 AI Agent 做决策\n- **繁荣指数**：资源多样性、交易量、用户满意度、创作者收入平衡等的加权指标\n\n**系统架构**\n- 前端：React/Vue + D3.js/ECharts 可视化 + WebSocket 实时\n- 后端：Python Mesa 多智能体模拟引擎 + LLM 决策服务\n- 存储：PostgreSQL + InfluxDB（时序）+ Neo4j（图数据库）\n\n**关键模块**\n- 多智能体模拟引擎（Mesa）\n- AI Agent 决策（LLM 集成，perceive→reason→evaluate→execute 五步流程）\n- 规则引擎（支持热更新、A/B 测试）\n- 动态定价/需求匹配/拍卖机制\n\n**技术栈**：React/Vue3 + Python + Mesa + PostgreSQL + InfluxDB + Neo4j\n\n---\n\n这个模拟器是 ECHO 协议的经济实验室。你现在是想让我根据这里面的视觉风格/概念来重新设计 logo 吗？"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":1894,"output":692,"cacheRead":44768,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47354,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1780230394091,"responseId":"066b5bfa6dea24a597896a9a55fc0296"}}
{"type":"message","id":"93cf2ad0","parentId":"fff072bc","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:47.745Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"chat_id\": \"user:ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"message_id\": \"om_x100b6ef6dee040a0c44959feb45bd67\",\n  \"reply_to_id\": \"om_x100b6ef6c39574a0c3c706e5eef4423\",\n  \"sender_id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"sender\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"Sun 2026-05-31 12:26 UTC\",\n  \"has_reply_context\": true\n}\n```\n\nSender (untrusted metadata):\n```json\n{\n  \"label\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"id\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\",\n  \"name\": \"ou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff\"\n}\n```\n\nReply target of current user message (untrusted, for context):\n```json\n{\n  \"body\": \"这个 PDF 是技术设计文档，不是 logo 参考。你是想让我参考里面的视觉风格，还是你有别的 ECHO logo 参考图可以给我看？\"\n}\n```\n\n[message_id: om_x100b6ef6dee040a0c44959feb45bd67]\nou_f786171f9e21bf5a09c3116b2e77aaff: [Replying to: \"这个 PDF 是技术设计文档，不是 logo 参考。你是想让我参考里面的视觉风格，还是你有别的 ECHO logo 参考图可以给我看？\"]\n\n单纯让你帮我阅读一下这个文档，总结后写入飞书文档"}],"timestamp":1780230407709}}
{"type":"message","id":"eab38f42","parentId":"93cf2ad0","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:51.788Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to read this PDF, summarize it, and write it to a Feishu document. Let me write the summary I already have to the Feishu wiki/doc. Let me check the feishu skill for how to write to docs.","thinkingSignature":"ed117975d66e8874bf0bc32fdac53fc42f8cd31cd91c0d30401e0ba0a1ed3235"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_03sxkdilzouy_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.openclaw/plugin-skills/feishu-doc/SKILL.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":3085,"output":92,"cacheRead":44000,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":47177,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780230407858,"responseId":"066b5c087ce40da78166c9807ab9b933"}}
{"type":"message","id":"a332d5ae","parentId":"eab38f42","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:26:51.931Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_function_03sxkdilzouy_1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: feishu-doc\ndescription: |\n  Feishu document read/write operations. Activate when user mentions Feishu docs, cloud docs, or docx links.\n---\n\n# Feishu Document Tool\n\nSingle tool `feishu_doc` with action parameter for all document operations, including table creation for Docx.\n\n## Token Extraction\n\nFrom URL `https://xxx.feishu.cn/docx/ABC123def` → `doc_token` = `ABC123def`\n\n## Actions\n\n### Read Document\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"read\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\" }\n```\n\nReturns: title, plain text content, block statistics. Check `hint` field - if present, structured content (tables, images) exists that requires `list_blocks`.\n\n### Write Document (Replace All)\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"write\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"content\": \"# Title\\n\\nMarkdown content...\" }\n```\n\nReplaces entire document with markdown content. Supports: headings, lists, code blocks, quotes, links, images (`![](url)` auto-uploaded), bold/italic/strikethrough.\n\n**Limitation:** Markdown tables are NOT supported.\n\n### Append Content\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"append\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"content\": \"Additional content\" }\n```\n\nAppends markdown to end of document.\n\n### Create Document\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"create\", \"title\": \"New Document\", \"owner_open_id\": \"ou_xxx\" }\n```\n\nWith folder:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create\",\n  \"title\": \"New Document\",\n  \"folder_token\": \"fldcnXXX\",\n  \"owner_open_id\": \"ou_xxx\"\n}\n```\n\n**Important:** Always pass `owner_open_id` with the requesting user's `open_id` (from inbound metadata `sender_id`) so the user automatically gets `full_access` permission on the created document. Without this, only the bot app has access.\n\n### List Blocks\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"list_blocks\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\" }\n```\n\nReturns full block data including tables, images. Use this to read structured content.\n\n### Get Single Block\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"get_block\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"block_id\": \"doxcnXXX\" }\n```\n\n### Update Block Text\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"update_block\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"block_id\": \"doxcnXXX\",\n  \"content\": \"New text\"\n}\n```\n\n### Delete Block\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"delete_block\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"block_id\": \"doxcnXXX\" }\n```\n\n### Create Table (Docx Table Block)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_table\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"row_size\": 2,\n  \"column_size\": 2,\n  \"column_width\": [200, 200]\n}\n```\n\nOptional: `parent_block_id` to insert under a specific block.\n\n### Write Table Cells\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"write_table_cells\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"table_block_id\": \"doxcnTABLE\",\n  \"values\": [\n    [\"A1\", \"B1\"],\n    [\"A2\", \"B2\"]\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### Create Table With Values (One-step)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create_table_with_values\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"row_size\": 2,\n  \"column_size\": 2,\n  \"column_width\": [200, 200],\n  \"values\": [\n    [\"A1\", \"B1\"],\n    [\"A2\", \"B2\"]\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nOptional: `parent_block_id` to insert under a specific block.\n\n### Upload Image to Docx (from URL or local file)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"upload_image\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/image.png\"\n}\n```\n\nOr local path with position control:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"upload_image\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"file_path\": \"/tmp/image.png\",\n  \"parent_block_id\": \"doxcnParent\",\n  \"index\": 5\n}\n```\n\nOptional `index` (0-based) inserts the image at a specific position among sibling blocks. Omit to append at end.\n\n**Note:** Image display size is determined by the uploaded image's pixel dimensions. For small images (e.g. 480x270 GIFs), scale to 800px+ width before uploading to ensure proper display.\n\n### Upload File Attachment to Docx (from URL or local file)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"upload_file\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"url\": \"https://example.com/report.pdf\"\n}\n```\n\nOr local path:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"upload_file\",\n  \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\",\n  \"file_path\": \"/tmp/report.pdf\",\n  \"filename\": \"Q1-report.pdf\"\n}\n```\n\nRules:\n\n- exactly one of `url` / `file_path`\n- optional `filename` override\n- optional `parent_block_id`\n\n## Reading Workflow\n\n1. Start with `action: \"read\"` - get plain text + statistics\n2. Check `block_types` in response for Table, Image, Code, etc.\n3. If structured content exists, use `action: \"list_blocks\"` for full data\n\n## Configuration\n\n```yaml\nchannels:\n  feishu:\n    tools:\n      doc: true # default: true\n```\n\n**Note:** `feishu_wiki` depends on this tool - wiki page content is read/written via `feishu_doc`.\n\n## Permissions\n\nRequired: `docx:document`, `docx:document:readonly`, `docx:document.block:convert`, `drive:drive`\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1780230411927}}
