{"type":"message","id":"e96a0bb2","parentId":"6570b101","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:27:11.273Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The error says \"Bad Request\". Let me check the API. The owner_open_id might not be the right parameter. Let me look at the feishu doc API more carefully.\n\nActually the issue might be that I need to use a different API. Let me check what parameters are needed for creating a doc.\n\nActually, thinking about it - since I'm in a Feishu DM with the user, I should just create the doc directly in the user's space. But wait - the error might be because I'm not passing the correct parameter name. \n\nLooking at the feishu-doc skill, the create action says:\n```json\n{\n  \"action\": \"create\",\n  \"title\": \"New Document\",\n  \"owner_open_id\": \"ou_xxx\"\n}\n```\n\nBut maybe I should use the `feishu_doc` tool instead of raw API calls. Actually the skill says it uses the feishu_doc tool, but looking at the available tools, I don't have a `feishu_doc` tool listed. \n\nSo I'm using the Node.js approach. The issue might be that the API for creating docx documents uses `/open-apis/docx/v1/documents` but requires a different request body format. Let me check the API docs.\n\nActually, the error code 9499 seems to indicate a parameter error. \n\nI think the problem is I'm passing `owner_open_id` as a top-level field when the API expects it nested under `folder_token`. Let me restructure the request with the proper hierarchy - putting `title` and `owner_open_id` at the top level, but I should verify the exact API requirements first.\n\nWait, looking at the feishu-doc skill more carefully, it mentions using `folder_token` for creating documents within a specific folder. I should try the `feishu_doc` tool directly since it's available to me, rather than making raw API calls.\n","thinkingSignature":"6b04435042f9e0a5ff33ad9c3869f441a9d4e5a3da77d5912f25d6c8d0292b76"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_rgvx7xuehqo2_1","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"node -e \"\nconst https = require('https');\nconst token = 't-g1045vjvHK6K342WLWHKAGPZDPCNBFSXPOISJX6T';\nconst body = JSON.stringify({\n  title: 'ECHO System Simulator 设计文档'\n});\nconst opts = { hostname: 'open.feishu.cn', path: '/open-apis/docx/v1/documents', method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Content-Length': body.length, 'Authorization': '***' + token } };\nconst req = https.request(opts, res => { let d = ''; res.on('data', c => d += c); res.on('end', () => { console.log(JSON.stringify(JSON.parse(d), null, 2)); }); });\nreq.write(body); req.end();\n\""}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":352,"output":586,"cacheRead":48736,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":49674,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780230425313,"responseId":"066b5c1ae18e9dac16c91c100a53012c"}}
