{"type":"message","id":"7103d4a9","parentId":"89f4f74b","timestamp":"2026-05-31T12:27:56.632Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The feishu_doc write action should use the `doc_token` + `/blocks` endpoint with a POST. Let me check the correct API endpoint. The feishu-doc skill says:\n\n```json\n{ \"action\": \"write\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"content\": \"# Title\\n\\nMarkdown content...\" }\n```\n\nSo the write action replaces the entire document. But I need to know the correct API endpoint for writing content. Let me check what the actual API call looks like for the write action.\n\nFrom the skill: `\"action\": \"write\", \"doc_token\": \"ABC123def\", \"content\": \"# Title\\n\\nMarkdown content...\"`\n\n\nI'm looking at the feishu open-apis documentation to find the correct endpoint for the docx write action, since the current approach with `/documents/{doc_token}/blocks` isn't working.","thinkingSignature":"635b18b0da7d0bc1802a60252c78cf89dbffea7c8252253627832078fa97ea03"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_88aex5b0kl5i_1","name":"tavily_search","arguments":{"query":"feishu open-apis docx v1 documents write content blocks api endpoint"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":400,"output":220,"cacheRead":55328,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":55948,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1780230471621,"responseId":"066b5c486d21482c0e88dd98721beaa1"}}
